From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 21:22:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Linux host: aot_lift lifts the functions a build lacks in
 groups of 32 per remill-lift process (#18)

A remill-lift run spends about 85 ms of a 90 ms lift loading the architecture
semantics. With Remill patch 0011 (remill-lift --batch) the semantics are
loaded once and each function is lifted by a forked copy. Aot now sends the
functions the cache lacks to the lifter 32 at a time, spread over the pool.
A function the batch cannot do is lifted again alone, AOT_LIFT_BATCH=0 turns
it off, and a lifter without --batch is detected on first use. The objects
are the same byte for byte, so the cache keys do not change. A cold build of
400 generated functions goes from 68 s to 31.6 s of CPU.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: Batch lifting: one remill-lift process for many functions, needs Remill patch 0011
Issue: Sunshine-Off/NX2Linux#18

